      "explanation": "Substituting \\(y=-8\\) makes the exponent on \\(5\\) zero:\n\\[\n5^{y+8}=5^{-8+8}=5^0=1.\n\\]\nThe equation therefore becomes \\(8\\cdot2^x=1\\), so\n\\[\n2^x=\\frac18=\\frac1{2^3}=2^{-3}.\n\\]\nSince powers of \\(2\\) increase with the exponent, equal values have equal exponents. Thus \\(x=-3\\), choice B.",
